@startuml context-map
title Model relations across bounded contexts

' Internal structure: UML/<context>/domain/relations.puml
' Purchase status order: UML/card/domain/purchase-status.puml
' Audit names every aggregate: UML/audit/domain/relations.puml

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam nodesep 40
hide empty members

package customer {
  class Customer
}

package merchant {
  class Merchant
}

package card {
  class Card
  class Purchase
  class AuthorizationHold
}

package settlement {
  class ClearingItem
  class Settlement
}

package ledger {
  class Account
  class JournalEntry
}

package audit {
  class AuditEvent
}

Customer "0..1" --> "1" Account : deposit account
Merchant "0..1" --> "1" Account : deposit account
Card "1" --> "1" Customer : holder

Purchase "1" <-- "0..1" ClearingItem : purchase
AuthorizationHold "1" <-- "0..1" ClearingItem : hold
Purchase "1" <-- "0..1" Settlement : purchase

AuthorizationHold ..> Account : available balance\n(derived)
Purchase ..> JournalEntry : customer posting\n2100 → 2300
Settlement ..> JournalEntry : merchant settlement\n2300 → 2200 + 4100

legend right
  Solid arrow = the source holds that reference.
  Crossing a package does not share a table.
  Dashed arrow = the purchase walk depends on the target.
  Audit names every aggregate in its own diagram.
  |= Context |= Owns |
  | ledger | Account, JournalEntry, JournalLine |
  | customer | Customer |
  | merchant | Merchant |
  | card | Card, Purchase, AuthorizationHold |
  | settlement | ClearingItem, Settlement |
  | audit | AuditEvent |
endlegend

note bottom of AuditEvent
  Append-only record of every mutation.
  aggregate_type + aggregate_id name
  Account, Customer, Merchant, JournalEntry,
  Card, Purchase, AuthorizationHold,
  ClearingItem, or Settlement.
  purchase_id is set for a purchase stage
  and null for a seed row.
end note

note as Boundaries
  PurchaseService is the only type that walks a purchase.
  It calls card, settlement, ledger, and audit in order.
  Contexts do not reach into each other's tables.
  shared has no model relations (API errors and the seeder runner).
end note

@enduml
